.TH WB\-REVERT 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-revert \- take an issue back to before a step
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR revert (<issue> | \-\-change <n>) <role> [\-\-round <n>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Take an issue back to before a step, deleting nothing: wb revert <issue> <role> [\-\-round <n>] posts, by issue_comment of watchbill.yml, one comment whose first line is [revert] <role> round <n>, for the last stamp of the role, or round <n>. From that stamp up to the marker no stamp, question or answer counts, for wb start <role>, wb prompt and wb status. wb revert \-\-change <n> <role> posts it on a change with no issue, by change_comment.
.PP
The branch, the issue's file and its acceptance, and the change are not touched: taking commits back is git's. The planner is taken back with git, not by a marker. Ends with 0 when the marker is posted, 1 when it was refused or the posting failed, 2 when it was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-round <n>
Take it back to the stamp of this round.
.TP
.B \-\-change <n>
Post the marker on a change with no issue, by change_comment.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The marker is posted.
.TP
.B 1
It was refused or the posting failed.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wb (1) ,
.BR wb\-start (1) ,
.BR wb\-status (1)
